-- | A formatted file's text with its trailing blank lines removed, leaving
-- | exactly one final newline.
-- |
-- | Leaf 1's three file-level rules survive leaf 2 as consequences of printing
-- | rather than as code — except this one, because a `BlankLines` trivium at
-- | the end of a file is indistinguishable from one between an item and an
-- | end-of-file comment until the whole text exists.
-- |
-- | Skipping every trailing `BlankLines` instead was the first attempt, and it
-- | lost the blank line before the final comment in `examples/comments.sdx` —
-- | the file whose subject is comments. So the decision is made on the output,
-- | where the difference is visible, rather than on the trivium, where it is
-- | not.
export(crate) trimmed_tail : String -> String
trimmed_tail text =
  mut text = text
  while .ends_with "\n\n" text
    .pop text
  text
